---
import Desktop from "../layouts/Desktop.astro";
import { pageOf } from "../data/pages";
import { orgNode, webPage, breadcrumbs } from "../data/schema";

const page = pageOf("/install/");
const jsonLd = [
  webPage({ path: "/install/", name: page.title, description: page.description, updated: new Date(page.updated) }),
  breadcrumbs([{ name: "Home", path: "/" }, { name: "Install", path: "/install/" }]),
  orgNode,
];
---
<Desktop title={page.title} description={page.description} page="install" headline="Install cl_quick on a Mac" jsonLd={jsonLd} ogImage="/og/install.png">
  <p class="readout"><span class="led lit" aria-hidden="true"></span><b>The first release isn't out yet.</b> There is nothing to download so far. Until there is, this page says what the Claude quick chat needs and how it works with Claude Code.</p>

  <div class="cols">
    <div class="col-stack">
      <div class="card">
        <h4>Requirements</h4>
        <ul class="list">
          <li><b>An Apple silicon Mac.</b></li>
          <li><b>macOS 13 or later.</b></li>
          <li><b>Claude Code, signed in.</b> cl_quick answers with your own Claude Code sign-in, so a profile needs a Claude Code folder that is signed in. <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/setup">Claude Code's setup guide</a> covers installing and signing in.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h4>How it works with Claude Code</h4>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li><b>A profile is a Claude Code folder.</b><span><code>~/.claude</code>, a <code>~/.claude-*</code> folder, or any folder set with <code>CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR</code>. On its first run cl_quick takes every signed-in one it finds, named after the folder.</span></li>
          <li><b>The bar opens, and a <code>claude</code> starts.</b><span>One <code>claude</code> at a time, on the profile's account in use. It is kept while a chat is open and ended after 15 minutes idle.</span></li>
          <li><b>Your Claude Code answers.</b><span>Each chat counts against that account's limits. Claude Code runs with no tools, no MCP servers and no settings files, and with its non-essential traffic (telemetry, error reports, update checks) off.</span></li>
          <li><b>The limits come from the same <code>claude</code>.</b><span>It is asked for the account's 5-hour and weekly limits, which sends nothing to a model, and the chat shows them in its top line.</span></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-stack">
      <div class="card">
        <h4>When the first release is out</h4>
        <p class="t">cl_quick isn't signed with an Apple Developer ID yet, so the first time it opens, macOS says it can't verify the app. Open System Settings ▸ Privacy &amp; Security and click <b>Open Anyway</b>, once.</p>
        <p class="t">The shortcut is <span class="kbd">⌥Space</span> by default, and <b>Open at login</b> in Settings ▸ General keeps cl_quick in the menu bar, ready for it.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h4>Already use cl_audit?</h4>
        <p class="t">cl_quick is the successor of <a href="https://cl-audit.n-uf.com">cl_audit</a>'s quick chat. On its first run it copies cl_audit's old quick chat settings (the shortcut, model and thinking), if there are any, and it shares nothing with cl_audit while running.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h4>Removing it</h4>
        <p class="t">Settings ▸ General ▸ Files ▸ <b>Remove cl_quick data…</b> moves cl_quick's folder and any old chats to the Trash, turns the login item off and quits. Your Claude Code folders, their sign-ins and their other sessions stay.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h4>Questions</h4>
        <p class="t">What cl_quick keeps and sends, what incognito means and how accounts switch are in the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a>. The <a href="/">home page</a> shows it working, step by step.</p>
        <p class="t">cl_quick is made by <a href="https://n-uf.com">n-uf</a> and is not affiliated with Anthropic.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Desktop>
